# strings it

## Objective
Extract readable strings from a binary file to find the hidden flag.

## Solution

```bash
cd /mnt/c/Users/delic/Downloads
strings "strings (1)" | grep picoCTF
```

The flag was found inside the printable strings of the binary.

## What I Learned

- How to use the `strings` command.
- How to filter output using `grep`.
- How to access Windows files from WSL using `/mnt/c/`.
